1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,950
The evil eye is real.

2
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:04,070
As the Prophet (peace be upon him) said in Sahih Muslim.

3
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:07,080
So how do we protect ourselves from the evil eye and envy?

4
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:10,640
Start by keeping up the morning and evening remembrances (adhkar),

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,160
and by reciting Ayat al-Kursi and the Mu‘awwidhat.

6
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:17,300
If you fear for yourself or for your child, say

7
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,190
what the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to recite to protect al-Hasan and al-Husayn:

8
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,910
“I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from every devil and every venomous creature,

9
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,740
and from every harmful evil eye.”

10
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:31,300
When you see something you admire — wealth, a child, a blessing — say:

11
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,780
“Mā shā’ Allāh. Tabārak Allāh. O Allah, bless it.”

12
00:00:35,210 --> 00:00:37,190
This is one of the greatest means of prevention.

13
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:41,950
If the evil eye does strike you, recite al-Fatiha and the Mu‘awwidhat over yourself,

14
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:45,610
place your hand on the spot of pain, and say “Bismillah” three times,

15
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:50,870
then say: “I seek refuge in the might and power of Allah from the evil of what I feel and what I fear” — seven times.

16
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:55,340
And take the means of treatment too — see a doctor if the symptoms persist.

17
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:57,830
Share this clip with someone who needs it

18
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,800
and save it so you can come back to it.

